.TH TAC 1.SH NAMEtac \- print a file last line first.SH SYNOPSIS\fBtac\fR[\-br] [\-s separator] [file ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBtac\fRis GNU tac, from the textutils: cat backwards.  It copies each namedfile, or the standard input, to the standard output with its records inreverse order.  A record ends at a line end unless\fB\-s\fRnames another separator..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-s\fI separator\fRrecords end at\fIseparator\fRinstead of at a line end.  Long form\fB+separator=\fIsep\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-b\fRthe separator belongs to the START of each record rather than the end.Long form\fB+before\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-r\fRthe separator is a regular expression.  Long form\fB+regex\fR.\fR.SH EXAMPLES.nftac notes               the last line firsttac log > recent        a log, newest entry firsttac -s e notes          reversed around every `e'.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOhead, tail, sort